The issue is that the values you use in the plot are not in the same scale as the values you give to FindFit.

In particular, your peak offset guess of `centrepeak = -91` should be on the same scale as the frequency variable used in the fit, i.e. something like `-2 π 91 10^3`, not just `-91`.

Similarly, the fit should be done with the same frequency scaling that you use when plotting, for example by fitting against `2 π Δ 10^3`.

A consistent version is:

```mathematica
scandata = Import["peakdata.csv"];
scandata = Map[{#[[1]], N[ToExpression[#[[2]]]]} &, scandata];

P1[Ω_, Δ_, t_] := ((Ω/Sqrt[Ω^2 + Δ^2])*Sin[(1/2)*Sqrt[Ω^2 + Δ^2]*t])^2;

fitfunction[Ω_, Δ_, t_, a_, b_, c_] := a + b*P1[Ω, Δ + c, t];

Ωapprox = 2 π 29 10^3;
centrepeak = -2 π 91 10^3;
amplitude = 0.8;
offset = 0.13;
pulsetime = 16*10^-6;

rabifit = 
 FindFit[
  scandata,
  {fitfunction[Ω, 2 π Δ 10^3, pulsetime, voffset, amp, hoffset],
   amp < 1, amp > 0, voffset > 0, voffset < 0.5},
  {{Ω, Ωapprox}, {amp, amplitude}, {voffset, offset}, {hoffset, centrepeak}},
  Δ,
  MaxIterations -> 1000
 ]
```

Then plot using the same scaling:

```mathematica
Show[
 Plot[{
   fitfunction[Ωapprox, 2 π Δ 10^3, pulsetime, offset, amplitude, centrepeak],
   fitfunction[Ω, 2 π Δ 10^3, pulsetime, voffset, amp, hoffset] /. rabifit},
  {Δ, 0, 200},
  PlotRange -> {All, {0, 1}},
  PlotStyle -> {Directive[Thick, Red], Directive[Thick, Orange]},
  Frame -> True
 ],
 ListPlot[scandata, PlotStyle -> PointSize[0.007]]
]
```

So the closest guidance is: make sure the parameter initial guesses and the fitted variable are expressed in the same units/scaling everywhere.

