For your function, if you want the roots of `B(z) == 1`, this works:

```mathematica
ClearAll[z]
b = (z (z - 0.5) (z + 0.5))/((1 - 0.5 z) (1 + 0.5 z));

sol = z /. NSolve[b == 1, z];
data = {Re[#], Im[#]} & /@ sol;

Graphics[
 {
  Circle[{0, 0}, 1],
  PointSize[.03],
  Red,
  Point[data],
  Line[Join[data, {First@data}]]
 },
 Axes -> True
]
```

If you want them ordered by angle around the origin, sort them first:

```mathematica
ClearAll[z]
b = (z (z - 0.5) (z + 0.5))/((1 - 0.5 z) (1 + 0.5 z));

sol = z /. NSolve[b == 1, z];
angles = Arg /@ sol;
data = ({Re[#], Im[#]} &) /@ sol[[Ordering[angles]]];

Graphics[
 {
  Circle[{0, 0}, 1],
  PointSize[.03],
  Red,
  Point[data],
  Line[Join[data, {First@data}]]
 },
 Axes -> True
]
```

