If you’re working with a vector-valued state in `NDSolve`, `WhenEvent` can’t test the whole vector with `y[t] == 0`. The supported approach shown here is to test a scalar condition, such as a norm or one component of the vector.

For example, this uses a threshold on the distance from a target vector and then resets `y[t]`:

```wl
s = NDSolve[
  {
    y'[t] == {{.1, -.2}, {-.1, .2}}.y[t],
    y[0] == {1, 1},
    WhenEvent[Norm[y[t] - {0.9460552574072016`, 1.053944742592798`}] <= .01,
      y[t] -> {1, 1}
    ]
  },
  y[t],
  {t, 0, 1}
]
```

So, if your goal is “replace values above a threshold with 1,” the closest supported pattern is to trigger the event with a scalar test such as a component condition or a norm-based condition, and then assign the new vector value in the event action.

