Since the system is linear, you do not need a numerical bifurcation diagram to assess stability. You can write it as

dp/dt = m.p

with

m = {{-10^12, -1, 0}, {1, -10^12, a}, {0, -a, 0}}.

The stability is determined by the eigenvalues of m. For example:

sol = Eigenvalues[m];

At sample values:

sol /. {a -> 0}
gives
{0, -1000000000000 - I, -1000000000000 + I}

sol /. {a -> -0.1}
gives
{-1.*10^12, -1.*10^12, -1.*10^-14}

sol /. {a -> 0.1}
gives
{-1.*10^12, -1.*10^12, -1.*10^-14}

So the system is stable for all values of a except a = 0, where it is marginally stable.

