Yes. The main speed issue in your code is the combination of Table and If inside nested loops.

The closest faster approach supported here is to avoid generating each result with repeated If tests and instead reorganize the computation so the values are sorted once and accumulated. In the accepted solution, that idea is implemented in a function like process2, which is much faster than the original Table/If version.

