Use a delayed rule, :>, instead of ->.

With ->, the right-hand side is evaluated before the pattern variables are substituted, so amp and afreq stay symbolic. With :>, the right-hand side is evaluated after the match, so the matched values are passed in.

For example:

s = {10 Cos[-Pi t], -4 Sin[0.23 t]};
f2[a1_, a2_, a3_] := Module[{a = a1, phi = a3}, Function[a a2[phi #1]]];
f1 := Function[f2[#1, #2, #3]];

l = Cases[s, amp_ trig_[afreq_ t] :> f1[amp, trig, afreq]];
%[[1]][.33]

This gives a numeric result.

So the key point is:

- -> for immediate rule evaluation
- :> for delayed evaluation, when you want the matched expressions inserted first

