For a list of ordered 3D points, you can detect where the coordinate relative to the plane changes sign between consecutive points, then linearly interpolate the crossing point. For the example plane z = 0.5, use the z-values:

zeroCrossings[l_List] := Module[{t, u, v},
  t = {Sign[l], Range[Length[l]]} // Transpose;
  u = Select[t, First[#] != 0 &];
  v = Split[u, First[#1] == First[#2] &];
  {Most[Max[#[[All, 2]]] & /@ v], Rest[Min[#[[All, 2]]] & /@ v]} // Transpose
]

