For Plot3D, the built-in AxesLabel option does not place the labels at the ends of the 3D axes the way you want. The supported workaround is to turn off the box and add your own labels with Graphics3D using Scaled positions.

Example:

Show[
  {
    Plot3D[x^2 + y^2 + 3, {x, -3, 3}, {y, -3, 3},
      AxesOrigin -> {0, 0, 0}, PlotRange -> {-1, 20}],
    Graphics3D[{
      Text["x", Scaled[{-.05, .5, 0}], {0, -1}],
      Text["y", Scaled[{.5, -.05, 0}], {0, -1}],
      Text["z", Scaled[{.5, .5, 1.1}]]
    }]
  },
  Boxed -> False
]

This places the x, y, and z labels near the ends of the drawn axes rather than clustered at the origin.

