The issue is that `AppendTo[ls, k++]` changes `ls`, and since the displayed `Dynamic` depends on `ls`, that triggers an immediate refresh. So the update interval gets bypassed by the dependency cycle.

To prevent that, make the dynamic ignore tracked symbols:

```wl
Dynamic[
  Refresh[
    AppendTo[ls, k++];
    Last@ls,
    UpdateInterval -> 10
  ],
  TrackedSymbols -> {}
]
```

This way, the display updates on the refresh interval instead of instantly responding to changes in `ls`.

The problem is that wrapping the function application in Dynamic and Function is getting in the way. Dynamic is meant for UI updating, not for being part of the expression you are trying to compute, and Function localizes its arguments so the symbols in your entered formula may not match what you think they are.

A simpler working approach is to store the entered formula in one variable and substitute the current x and y values into it:

DynamicModule[{dydx = Null, xi = Null, yi = Null},
  Deploy @ Panel @ Grid @ Transpose @
   {
    {"Differential equation: (dy/dx)=", "x:", "y:", "slope:"},
    {
     InputField[Dynamic[dydx]],
     InputField[Dynamic[xi]],
     InputField[Dynamic[yi]],
     InputField[Dynamic[dydx /. {x -> xi, y -> yi}], Enabled -> False]
    }
   }
]

