You can get to the parent cell by moving the notebook selection to the current evaluation cell, then walking to the first cell of its cell group. Once the selection is on that cell, `CurrentValue` can read its options.

For example:

```wl
parentcell[] := Module[{cellstyle, nb},
  nb = EvaluationNotebook[];
  SelectionMove[nb, All, EvaluationCell];
  firstcell[nb];
  cellstyle = NotebookRead[nb][[2]];

  If[cellstyle == "Input",
    SelectionMove[nb, All, CellGroup];
    firstcell[nb]
  ]
]

firstcell[nb_] := (
  SelectionMove[nb, All, CellGroup];
  SelectionMove[nb, Before, CellGroup];
  SelectionMove[nb, Next, Cell]
)
```

Then you can access the parent cell’s options like this:

```wl
