CurrentValue[NotebookSelection[EvaluationNotebook[]], CellTags]
```

If you want to keep moving upward until you reach a cell of a particular style, such as `"Section"`, you can use:

```wl
parentcell[style_String] := Module[{nb},
  nb = EvaluationNotebook[];
  SelectionMove[nb, All, EvaluationCell];
  firstcell[nb];

  While[NotebookRead[nb][[2]] =!= style,
    SelectionMove[nb, All, CellGroup];
    firstcell[nb]
  ]
]
```

This works by traversing the notebook structure from the current evaluation cell upward through cell groups. It has some odd behavior in notebooks without real hierarchy beyond input/output grouping: the selection may end up at the input cell or at the first cell in the notebook.

