  {
    x''[t] + c x'[t] + Sin[x[t]] + f Cos[w t] == 0,
    x'[0] == 0,
    x[0] == 1
  },
  x,
  {t, 0, 10},
  {w}
];

Manipulate[
  With[{x1 = x[w] /. sol},
    Plot[x1[t], {t, 0, 10}, PlotRange -> All, AxesLabel -> {"t", "x"}]
  ],
  {w, 0.1, 1.5}
]
```

This works because `ParametricNDSolve` returns a solution depending on `w`, and `x[w] /. sol` gives the corresponding interpolating function for each slider value.

Your original code does not work well because `NDSolve` is being called with `w` left symbolic, and `soln := ...` is recomputed in a way that does not correctly tie the solution to the slider value.

