The fastest approach shown in the thread is to avoid the original nested Table/Sum form and instead use a more compact accumulation-based method.

For a single pair of vector and weights, the improved version is:

process2[x_, w_, {y0_, dy_, ny_}] :=
  Module[{x0, w0},
    x0 = Ceiling[(x - y0)/dy] ~Clip~ {0, ny};
    x0 = Join[{0}, Sort @ x0, {ny}];
    w0 = {0} ~Join~ Accumulate[w[[Ordering @ x]]];
    Join @@ MapThread[ConstantArray, {w0, Differences@x0}]
  ]

