Using the provided tree-building function, you can do:

`makeRojoTree[words_List] :=
 StartOfString @@ 
  ReplaceRepeated[
    makeTree[words], {
      ({} -> {}) :> EndOfString,
      Rule[x_, l_List] :> x @@ l
    }
  ]`

This converts the root into `StartOfString[...]` and each rule like `"h" -> {...}` into `"h"[...]`, while `{} -> {}` becomes `EndOfString`.

For the sample input, this produces the same general tree structure you want, though the branch order may differ slightly. If needed, that ordering can be adjusted separately.

