Use `Epilog` to overlay the point and tangent on the curve, and make the tangent depend on the parameter so it updates as the parameter changes.

For a parameterized curve `{x[t], y[t]}`, you can compute the tangent direction from the derivative and draw a short line segment centered at the current point:

```wl
x[t_] := Cos[t];
y[t_] := Sin[t];

tangentSegment[t0_, d_] := Module[
  {p, v},
  p = {x[t0], y[t0]};
  v = {x'[t0], y'[t0]};
  {p - d v, p + d v}
];

Manipulate[
 Plot[{x[t], y[t]}, {t, 0, 2 Pi},
  Epilog -> {
    Red, PointSize[Large], Point[{x[t0], y[t0]}],
    Blue, Line[tangentSegment[t0, 0.3]]
  }
 ],
 {t0, 0, 2 Pi},
 SaveDefinitions -> True
]
```

